    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p6_b17",
      "text": "outperforms both baselines across nearly all metrics. The\nexception is the CHAIR score on the AMBER Generative\nTask and Object HalBench. We attribute this anomaly to a\nflaw in the CHAIR metric, which scores outputs by match-\ning generated object words to ground-truth objects. This\nscoring mechanism is susceptible to reward hacking; mod-\nels can artificially inflate their CHAIR score by repeatedly\ndescribing a few salient objects in the image. A more\nthorough discussion of the CHAIR metric\u2019s limitations is\nprovided in Section D.2.\n",
